   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/, per NSW Health's copyright
   statement at https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/pages/copyright.aspx.

   Changes made (CC BY 4.0, section 3(a)(1)(B)): the wording is
   reproduced unchanged. The nine sub-items of "Patient health summary"
   are listed and counted individually. NSW publishes the triage
   categories as a table; they are shown one category to a line, with
   dashes between the columns. NSW attaches a note to "Cardiovascular
   disease risk assessment" pointing to the Australian guideline and
   calculator for assessing and managing cardiovascular risk. Notes that
   NSW attaches to individual items are not reproduced. Spacing is
   normalised (the NSW page contains non-breaking and zero-width
   characters). The page's emergency criteria are not
   reproduced because the demonstration does not assess urgency. NSW
   Health has not reviewed or endorsed this demonstration.

   Dated snapshots of the same text, including the emergency criteria and
   the page headings, are kept in tests/fetched/ for the monthly
   consistency check, under the same licence and attribution.

   The result screen also quotes three passages from NSW Health,
   "Frequently asked questions about state-wide referral criteria" (page
   dated 6 June 2025),
   https://www.health.nsw.gov.au/outpatients/referrals/Pages/faqs.aspx,
   under the same copyright statement and licence. The passages are
   quoted unchanged; two are parts of sentences and one is a whole
   sentence. They were checked character for character against the page's
   HTML, saved by the author on 7 October 2026.

   data/nsw-chest-pain-adult.json reproduces the same NSW page as
   structured data, and additionally includes the page's emergency criteria,
   the note attached to "Cardiovascular disease risk assessment" and the
   "Important information" paragraph, under the same copyright statement
   and licence. Wording is unchanged; whitespace is collapsed, zero-width
   characters are removed, and lists and the table are represented as
   structured data.

2. Criteria of other Australian jurisdictions

   The Victorian Statewide Referral Criteria, Queensland Clinical
   Prioritisation Criteria and Western Australian Referral Access Criteria are
   not published under a licence that permits reproduction here, and are
   deliberately NOT reproduced in this repository. What each site's
   copyright statement said when read on 6 October 2026 is set out, with
   links, in docs/02-what-already-exists.md.

3. Software dependencies

   The demonstration page has no runtime dependencies. The test script
   tests/test_demo.js uses Playwright (Apache-2.0), which is not distributed
   with this repository; package.json names the version to install.

